# Allow-list ("gitallow") pattern: ignore everything, then re-admit exactly what
# belongs in the repository. A file that is not named below is not committed by
# accident — the failure mode of a deny-list, where a new build artefact or a
# stray credential slips in because nobody thought to exclude it.

# 1. Ignore everything, including inside directories.
/*
!/.gitignore

# 2. Re-admit the tracked top-level files.
!/.JuliaFormatter.toml
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/justfile
!/LICENSE.md
!/Project.toml
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/upstream-bugs.md

# 3. Re-admit the tracked directories, then their contents.
!/.github/
!/docs/
!/notebooks/
!/src/
!/test/

# 4. Inside those directories, exclude what is generated rather than authored.
#    Manifests are resolved per machine; the notebook and docs environments
#    both use `[sources]`, so nothing needs a committed Manifest.
Manifest.toml
/docs/build/
/docs/slate_cache/
/docs/src/notebooks/
/docs/src/llms.txt
/docs/src/llms-full.txt

# 5. Editor and OS noise, wherever it lands.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
